% Round-13 explore-completeness fixture — instant-feeding with PLAIN arcs.
% `make` (zero delay) produces b at the SAME instant, enabling `use`, which
% then races `eat` for c. The tied set {make, eat} shares no cohort, so the
% pre-round-13 partial-order reduction committed sorted-first ('eat') and
% never discovered the make→use world. exec (chooser) reaches both:
%   eat first:  { b, d }        make first, use wins c: { prize }
make: a -o { b }.
eat: c -o { d }.
use: b * c -o { prize }.
